  "solution": {
    "text": "Since friction absent, we can apply the law of conservation of energy. Centre of gravity of a semicircular arc is at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math> from the centre.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Initial potential energy</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">λ</mtext><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow><mtext>π</mtext></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Final potential energy</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">λ</mtext><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br />When the chain is completely slipped off the tube, all the links of the chain have the same velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>.<br /><br /><u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0082_f508caacdbf0.jpg\" /></strong></u><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Kinetic energy of chain</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">λ</mtext><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>From COE,</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">λ</mtext><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">rg</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>π</mtext></mrow><mtext>r</mtext></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">λ</mtext><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">g</mtext><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">λ</mtext><mtext>π</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>From which we find,</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"></mspace><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mtext>π</mtext></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mtext>π</mtext><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math>"
  }
